 # ClawVille — Architecture
 
+**Last Audited:** 2026-07-14 (26): **CLV live-swap depth hard-dependency removed locally; Fable staging proof pending, not shipped.** `clv-swap-live.ts` no longer requires DexScreener `poolLiquidityUsd` to execute cash-out rail ② or E3 redemption delivery. Each clip starts at `min(remaining, CLV_SWAP_JUPITER_PROBE_USDC)` (default/max $25; exact µUSDC parse, operators may tune down), validates the complete Jupiter ExactIn quote/echo/route, and accepts only that exact candidate's decimal-fraction `priceImpactPct <= CLV_SWAP_MAX_IMPACT_BPS/10_000`. Over-cap quotes are never signed: `nextµ=floor(currentµ × allowedImpact / observedImpact)`, additionally capped at `floor(currentµ/2)` for conservative bounded termination, then re-quoted down to 1 µUSDC; the accepted quote object is reused unchanged for `/swap`. Long Jupiter decimals are fixed-point CEILed at 18dp, so discarded precision cannot understate impact. A $P probe was deliberately NOT converted to depth: even for one fee-free balanced CPMM, exact both-side TVL is `L=2P(1-i)/i`; Jupiter split/multi-hop CLMM/DLMM routes do not satisfy that single-curve contract, so any inferred `L` can over-size a later clip. Dex depth remains a max-stale-gated, memory-only dry-run/advisory observation and never affects live liveness. `planClips`/`sizeClipMicro`, µUSD floor, oracle price/freshness+tolerance gate, Jupiter tx binding, and settle/reconcile machine are unchanged. Operator `live-tick-once.ts` now waits for fresh price only. No DDL/protocol/parity surface changed. **PARITY:** shared backend money executor; human cash-out and agent/human E3 redemption consume the identical guarded queue path.
+
 **Last Audited:** 2026-07-14 (25): **Tokenomics E1/E2 backing + sybil teeth and E3 EARNED exit rail — BUILT-GATED DARK, not migrated/deployed/signed off.** Additive idempotent migrations `0030a`/`0030b`/`0031` introduce the singleton `treasury_wallets(purpose='earned-backing')`, `earn_events`, wallet/first-funder cluster epoch counters, per-mint fungibility lots, physical `earned_backing`, exact lot consumption/accounted-ledger cutover repair, claw-backs, and the durable redemption/funding/delivery machine. Founder economics are integer exact: 1 vCLAW=$0.01=10,000 micro-USDC; E1 entry rake is zero; the loop's only fee is 444 bps at exit; net `amountVclaw×9556` micro-USDC market-buys floating-price CLV and conservative confirmed output is delivered to the earner's custodial ATA. Dead 40/20/30/10, dividend, P/E, reserve, and fixed-anchor models remain forbidden. E2 imports verify exact same-network inbound USDC plus current custody solvency under a shared custody mutex/advisory lock; pending mints are spendable but not redeemable; the job resolves payer age/history + first funder, cluster-caps sibling payers per earner/epoch, and transitions verified/rejected. Rejection releases backing without deleting spendability. Named-admin claw-back debits available EARNED, records deficit durably, marks the event, and releases unconsumed backing idempotently. Rail ④ agent-pay remains direct-to-recipient and therefore dual-writes `backing='none'`; making it cashable later requires re-routing payer USDC through backing custody. E3 `POST /api/tokenomics/redeem` + owner-scoped `GET /:id` use `requireAuthOrAgentSession`; human and ledger-capable bound agent resolve the same avatar/custodial wallet, guests/unbound refuse. State: requested/refused → debited → buy_queued → bought → delivering → delivered/reconcile; capture-before-send, CAS claims, exactly-once queue source, confirmed-slot RPC freshness, and ambiguous⇒reconcile inherit `docs/money-rails.md §3`. Route and every service/worker entry require literal `TOKENOMICS_REDEEM_ENABLED==='true'`, default OFF; G2 funded adversarial smoke and G3 founder legal/MSB/money-transmitter/KYC/sanctions clearance are launch prerequisites. Universal `clawville_redeem_earned` tools.json + protocol manual §14 move `PROTOCOL_VERSION 17→18`; Hatcher `[ACTION:]` whitelist and partner wire are unchanged (public ref cross-check `9cc426b…`, staging harness pending). **Drift note:** the Drizzle `earn_events.backing_network` type is narrowed to `'mainnet' | 'devnet'`, matching the existing `earn_events_backing_network_valid` CHECK; no DDL changed. **PARITY:** human path = same POST/GET via Lucia; agent path = same endpoints/tool via `X-Clawville-Agent-Session`; settlement binds middleware-resolved `identity.avatarId` and its server-resolved custodial wallet. Canonical ops/funding/solvency/reconcile/gas runbooks: `docs/money-rails.md`. No migrations were applied by this build.
 
 **Last Audited:** 2026-07-14 (24): **Money rails CLOSED — all four LIVE on prod** (`a0b43c1c`; `CLV_SWAP_EXECUTE=true` + `RECONCILE_APPLY=true` flipped, LIVE worker boot-verified; ② proven end-to-end on mainnet-staging with on-chain sigs). **Canonical ops reference: `docs/money-rails.md`** — wallet map (pubkeys, gas floors, key custody), settle-machine invariants, runbooks (gas funding, evidence-gated queue resets, reconcile CLI, deploy/flip verification), backup/recovery chain (`VANITY_ENCRYPTION_KEY` escrowed 2026-07-14 — was Coolify-only single point of failure). Read that doc before touching any money-path file. PARITY: docs-only entry.
